#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#This example has a front-facing sensor configured to only detect things down low. Moving point targets are defined to follow on lane edges at 5-m intevals in front of the sensor.
#
#A CarSim Sensors license is required to run this simulation.  You may still view the animation and plots.
#
#When traffic vehicles are included, the vehicles occlude some of the lane edge points.
#
#If traffic vehicles are included, the vehicles occlude some of the lane edge points.
#
#This example has lane detection for three edges that are defined using LTARG datasets.
#
#This example also has blind-spot detection sensors that generate HUD alerts when vehicles in the right lane enter the blind spot. Oncoming vehicles in the adjacent left lane are also detected, but the alerts are not shown because the signal is low-pass filtered to avoid flickering.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

